<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108864" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόνομ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονέμομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>undermined,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρα ὑ. πυρὶ καὶ ὕδατι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					12.8.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>underground,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τάφροι</span>”
				<i>sewers,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>BC</u>
					4.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρύγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					7.9.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἄντρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.1.67
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τὴν ἀποφορὰν ἔχει,</span>
			of a lake, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				12.8.19
			</span></i> (s. v. l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἕλκος</span> a <i>spreading</i>
			ulcer <i>with undermined edges,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλποι ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.128
				</span></i>
			, cf. Heras ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.815
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόνομος, ὁ,</span> as Subst., <i>underground passage,
				mine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.76
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι ὑπονόμοις, ἀλλ᾽ ἤδη μηχαναῖς
					αἱρεῖν τὴν πολιτείαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>waterpipe, conduit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.1.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				350a1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.2491.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				745.19
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>sewer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.3.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				4.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>vein</i> of minerals, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				4.26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
